## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical data structure design for a common gaming feature, balancing efficient updates with query performance.

## Key Concepts
- Hash maps provide O(1) player score lookups
- Ordered maps enable range and top-k access
- Ordered sets handle duplicate scores within groups
- Rank computation accounts for tied scores

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode illustrating approach
class Leaderboard {
  constructor(){
    this.playerToScore = new Map();
    this.scoreToPlayers = new Map(); // descending keys; each maps to a Set of players
  }
  addOrUpdate(playerId, score) {
    // Remove from old score group if exists
    const oldScore = this.playerToScore.get(playerId);
    if (oldScore !== undefined) {
      const oldSet = this.scoreToPlayers.get(oldScore);
      oldSet.delete(playerId);
      if (oldSet.size === 0) this.scoreToPlayers.delete(oldScore);
    }
    // Update maps and add to new score group
    this.playerToScore.set(playerId, score);
    if (!this.scoreToPlayers.has(score)) {
      this.scoreToPlayers.set(score, new Set());
    }
    this.scoreToPlayers.get(score).add(playerId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a mutable deque with constant-time min/max queries, a common interview pattern for surface-level data-structure mastery.

## Key Concepts
- Deque operations and invariants
- Two-stack technique for amortized efficiency
- Maintaining per-element min/max for O(1) queries
- Edge-case handling (empty, duplicates)

## Code Example
```javascript
class MinMaxDeque {
  constructor() {
    this.front = [];
    this.back = [];
  }
  pushFront(x) {
    const last = this.front[this.front.length - 1];
    const mn = last ? Math.min(x, last.min) : x;
    const mx = last ? Math.max(x, last.max) : x;
    this.front.push({ v: x, min: mn, max: mx });
  }
  pushBack(x) {
    const last = this.back[this.back.length - 1];
    const mn = last ? Math.min(x, last.min) : x;
    const mx = last ? Math.max(x, last.max) : x;
    this.back.push({ v: x, min: mn, max: mx });
  }
  popFront() {
    if (this.front.length === 0) {
      while (this.back.length) this.pushFront(this.back.pop().v);
    }
    if (this.front.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    return this.front.pop().v;
  }
  popBack() {
    if (this.back.length === 0) {
      while (this.front.length) this.pushBack(this.front.pop().v);
    }
    if (this.back.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    return this.back.pop().v;
  }
  getMin() {
    if (this.front.length === 0 && this.back.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    let mn = null;
    if (this.front.length) mn = this.front[this.front.length - 1].min;
    if (this.back.length) {
      const bmin = this.back[this.back.length - 1].min;
      mn = mn === null ? bmin : Math.min(mn, bmin);
    }
    return mn;
  }
  getMax() {
    if (this.front.length === 0 && this.back.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    let mx = null;
    if (this.front.length) mx = this.front[this.front.length - 1].max;
    if (this.back.length) {
      const bmax = this.back[this.back.length - 1].max;
      mx = mx === null ? bmax : Math.max(mx, bmax);
    }
    return mx;
  }
}
```

